WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:01.630
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
Today, we're talking

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:03.040
about Google
Cloud's Architecture

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.062
Framework, streaming
analytics, and Cloud OnBoard.

00:00:06.062 --> 00:00:08.020
I'm Mark Mirchandani,
and welcome to "This Week

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.450
in Cloud," where we serve
you the lowest latency

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:13.180
news from the safety of home.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.070
Google Cloud's
Architecture Framework

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:17.710
offers best practices and
implementation guidance

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:19.660
for your application design.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.430
From operational excellence
to security, privacy

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.630
and compliance, reliability,
and cost optimization,

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.120
this framework provides
strategies, recommendations,

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.770
and design questions
that will help

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:33.330
you build the architecture
you need to succeed.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.580
Google Cloud is bringing
together all of our streaming

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.710
technologies into one solution.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.050
Streaming analytics makes
data more organized,

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:43.110
useful, and accessible from
the instant it's generated.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:45.135
Built on Pub/Sub,
Dataflow, and BigQuery,

00:00:45.135 --> 00:00:47.010
our streaming solution
provides the resources

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.050
you need to ingest,
process, and analyze

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:52.050
fluctuating volumes of real
time data for real time business

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.072
insights.

00:00:53.072 --> 00:00:55.030
Check out the features
that make this possible,

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:57.750
and then build your
own streaming pipeline.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.280
Now could be a great
time to learn from home.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:02.910
You can tune in on
May 19 and 20 to watch

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.000
instructors on
Google Cloud OnBoard

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.380
break down what it takes
to migrate to Google Cloud

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.943
and explain the basics of
Google Kubernetes Engine.

00:01:09.943 --> 00:01:11.610
After the sessions,
you'll have a chance

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.340
to test what you've learned by
participating in hands-on labs

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.743
and challenges with the
Cloud Hero online challenge.

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:20.160
Have you ever wondered how
Google Cloud technical solution

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.770
engineers solve some
of your support cases?

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.870
Or maybe you're just a
fan of detective stories.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.510
Either way, we've got a fun
and informative deep-dive

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.370
into how one of our
engineers solved a DNS

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.037
problem for a customer.

00:01:31.037 --> 00:01:33.120
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.275
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:35.275 --> 00:01:36.400
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.110
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:40.670
We'll see you in the cloud.

